{"ref":"card:question","text":"Do CPU and GPU docking agree across 4 fixed cases and 50 ranked poses after independent numerical calibration?","sources":[]}
{"ref":"card:hypothesis","text":"Independent repeats and error analysis can justify CPU/GPU agreement before acceleration or denser search receives scientific interpretation.","sources":[]}
{"ref":"card:if_lever","text":"At 4 repeats, independent bounds support agreement for all 4 cases and 50 ranks; 2 repeats leave calibration unresolved.","sources":[]}
{"ref":"card:if_not","text":"At 4 repeats, agreement remains unresolved or fails, or 2 repeats already suffice; extra calibration buys no changed agreement decision.","sources":[]}
{"ref":"card:test_summary","text":"Build CPU-only subset/control harness, then calibrate 2 and 4 repeats per backend across 4 cases. Seal independent error bounds; compare 1 fresh CPU/GPU pair per case using all 50 ranks. Stop unresolved if bounds fail.","sources":[]}
{"ref":"card:closest_prior","text":"MEGADOCK authors report CPU/GPU precision differences without repeat counts; published parallel study measured docking scalability, not this calibration decision [faq] [paper].","sources":[{"id":"faq","url":"https://www.bi.cs.titech.ac.jp/megadock/faq.html","quote":"Answer: Because of precision of GPUs, the results of docking scores are slightly different by CPU version and GPU version."},{"id":"paper","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4221127/","quote":"Notably, a high scalability (98%) was obtained with the largest number of nodes (420 nodes)."}]}
{"ref":"card:left_open","text":"Whether 2 or 4 independent repeats plus audited error bounds support all 50 ranked poses across these 4 cases remains open.","sources":[]}
{"ref":"card:limits","text":"No density, speedup, biological efficacy or population claim. Four previously exposed cases only; absent independent numerical justification leaves agreement unresolved.","sources":[]}
{"ref":"src:faq","url":"https://www.bi.cs.titech.ac.jp/megadock/faq.html","quote":"Answer: Because of precision of GPUs, the results of docking scores are slightly different by CPU version and GPU version.","supports":"Precision differences motivate separate scientific tolerance; FAQ does not establish acceptance for these exact cases."}
{"ref":"src:paper","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4221127/","quote":"Notably, a high scalability (98%) was obtained with the largest number of nodes (420 nodes).","supports":"Search returned open full-text extraction of published parallel study. Different compute axis; neither repeat-count calibration nor case-specific agreement result."}

